In the discussion, James asked why Nicola Ranger is called "Professor." I explained that she holds the title of **Professor in Practice of Natural Capital, Risk and Finance** at the Grantham Research Institute, which is an academic position reflecting her distinguished real-world leadership and expertise rather than a conventional tenure-track role. I noted her qualifications, including her doctorate in Atmospheric Physics, extensive research, and experience with major institutions like the World Bank and various government entities, which validate her appointment.
